  "aiOverview": {
    "content": "A fillip (pronounced /ˈfɪl.ɪp/) is a stimulus, boost, or unexpected boost that encourages improvement or excitement. It also refers to a sharp, small tap made by snapping a finger against a thumb. Originating in the 15th century as a word for this finger-snap, it evolved to mean any small incentive. Usage Examples \"The tax reduction provided a much-needed fillip to the struggling housing market\". \"The surprise announcement gave her campaign a significant fillip\". \"The chef added a final fillip of parsley to the dish\". Synonyms Stimulus, boost, encouragement, incentive, impetus, fillip, stimulus, stimulant. Embellishment, addition, extra, twist, sparkle. Antonyms Block, check, discouragement, hindrance, deterrent.",
